I know it puts things into perspective  for me Julie Chrisley seemingly in  denial about her prison sentence we all  think our heart is the hardest thing on  the latest episode of Chrisley  confessions Julie's joined by her son  Chase's fiancee Emmy meters and the  reality star who's set to report to  prison this month with her husband Todd  reflects on having to spend years apart  from him there is that possibility of my  husband and I being separated  but there's a difference between my  husband and I being separated  for a period of time and having to say  goodbye forever the difference she's  referencing how seeing Emmy's mother  care for her father during his ALS  diagnosis put things into perspective so  it almost makes me feel  ashamed that I'm even worried you know  she's going to have to say goodbye to  her husband  [Music]  and she won't see him again this side of  Heaven  [Music]  and so I think it puts things into  perspective I made that commitment that  no matter how tough things were I was  not going to walk away and you know as  our marriage perfect no it's not but I  do think we have this mutual respect and  we both agree that we're not throwing in  the towel no matter how tough things get  and you know from a blended family to  having our own kids to just all the  drama that comes along with life it's  easy to do after being convicted of tax  fraud in June Julie sentenced to seven  years in prison and 16 months probation  while Todd sentenced to 12 years in  prison and 16 months probation I would  love to say it's all scripted but you  can't script the dysfunction that goes  on and on there's nothing else for you  to know about us it's all out there so  there's no bombshells according to docs  obtained by ET the couple's been ordered  to report to two different federal  prisons on January 17th what we will not  do is we will not break we made a  commitment that we were not going to  give up in the podcast Julie also gets  emotional when mentioning 